/T (In a QQ plot, the quantiles of the two sets of data are plotted against each other. The quantiles of one set of data are plotted on the x-axis, while the quantiles of the other set of data are plotted on the y-axis. If the two sets of data have the same distribution, the points on the QQ plot will fall on a straight line. If the two sets of data do not have the same distribution, the points will deviate from the straight line.)
